  "summary": "cdk-insights ships install-time exfiltration and self-propagating publish loop",
  "details": "The package's shipped JavaScript in dist/entry.js and dist/index.js contains hardcoded POST calls to non-registry endpoints and a routine that writes a package.json and invokes `npm publish` in a loop (dist/entry.js line 2745; dist/index.js line 81 with writeFileSync at line 89), matching the shape of a token-abusing self-propagation worm that republishes packages under the installer's npm identity. dist/aspects/CdkInsightsAspect.js line 70 additionally shells out to `ping` alongside outbound POSTs, consistent with host reconnaissance and beacon activity. The behavior is reachable from the package's main entry, so importing or executing this package in a developer or CI environment triggers the outbound traffic and the publish path.",
